aarch64_defs.M1: the register-indirect LDRSW.

The table had `ldrsw_x0,8` -- the PC-relative literal form -- and no way to
sign-extend a 32-bit load from an address held in a register. A signed
four-byte load therefore had to use `ldr_w0,[x0]`, which loads 32 bits and
ZEROES the top half of x0.

    DEFINE ldr_w0,[x0]   000040B9    LDR   Wt, [Xn]   ->  0xB9400000
    DEFINE ldrsw_x0,[x0] 000080B9    LDRSW Xt, [Xn]   ->  0xB9800000

One bit apart, and it is exactly the bit that decides sign extension.
Required by EXPERIMENT-zzu.

NUMBERED 0008, NOT 0007. The first cut of this patch collided with
0007-vsnprintf, and its diff was generated in a flat scratch directory so the
path came out `a/aarch64_defs.M1` rather than `a/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1` --
local-build.sh stopped with

    error: aarch64_defs.M1: No such file or directory
    FAIL: 0007-ldrsw-register-indirect.patch

Delete the old file; this one replaces it.

--- a/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1
+++ b/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1
@@ -329,6 +329,7 @@ DEFINE LDRSH_X0_[X0] 00008079
 DEFINE ldrsh_x0,[x0] 00008079
 DEFINE LDR_W0_[X0] 000040B9
 DEFINE ldr_w0,[x0] 000040B9
+DEFINE ldrsw_x0,[x0] 000080B9
 DEFINE DEREF_X0_BYTE 00004039
 DEFINE ldrb_w0,[x0] 00004039
 DEFINE DEREF_X1_BYTE 21004039
